nk</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microbial export of lactic and 3-hydroxypropanoic acid: implications for inductrial fermentation processes</article-title><source>Metab Eng</source><year>2004</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15491854</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ymben.2004.05.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bakker</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Overkamp</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>van Maris</surname><given-names>AJA</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000f6;tter</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Luttik</surname><given-names>MAH</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dijken</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Pronk</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stoichiometry and compartmentation of NADH metabolism in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>FEMS Microbiol Rev</source><year>2001</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11152939</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1574-6976.2001.tb00570.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rigoulet</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Aguilaniu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Av&#x000e9;ret</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunoust</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Camougrand</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Grandier-Vazeille</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pahlman</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Manon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gustafsson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organization and regulation of the cytosolic NADH metabolism in the yeast <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Mol Cell Biochem</source><year>2004</year><volume>256-257</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14977171</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/B:MCBI.0000009888.79484.fd</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weusthuis</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Visser</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Pronk</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheffers</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dijken</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of oxygen limitation on sugar metabolism in yeasts &#x02013; a continuous-culture study of the Kluyver effect</article-title><source>Microbiology</source><year>1994</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>703</fpage><lpage>715</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8012592</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franz&#x000e8;n</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metabolic flux analysis of RQ-controlled microaerobic ethanol production by <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Yeast</source><year>2003</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12518316</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/yea.956</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verduyn</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Postma</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheffers</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dijken</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physiology of <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae </italic>in anaerobic glucose-limited chemostat cultures</article-title><source>J Gen Microbiol</source><year>1990</year><volume>136</volume><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1975265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snoek</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Steensma</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors involved in anaerobic growth of <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Yeast</source><year>2007</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17192845</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/yea.1430</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gancedo</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Yeast carbon catabolite repression</article-title><source>Microbiol Mol Biol Rev</source><year>1998</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>334</fpage><lpage>361</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9618445</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Deken</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Crabtree effect: a regulatory system in yeast</article-title><source>J Gen Microbiol</source><year>1966</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5969497</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname